-- Conformance: a constructor pattern over a scrutinee whose type declares no
-- such constructor is a checker error (Chapter 4, Section 4.9.1).
-- Tests: E314 — `Some` and `None` are constructors of Option<T>, and the
-- scrutinee here is the Map<String, Int> that map_new() returns.  A Map is a
-- built-in container: it is an ADT with no constructors at all, so neither arm
-- can ever be taken.  The exhaustiveness pass cannot see this — a type with no
-- constructor registry reads to it as one it does not know — so the pattern is
-- typed against the scrutinee instead, once, for every pattern form (#1315).
public fn count(@Unit -> @Int)
  requires(true)
  ensures(true)
  effects(pure)
{
  match map_new() {
    Some(@Int) -> 1,
    None -> 2
  }
}

public fn main(@Unit -> @Int)
  requires(true)
  ensures(true)
  effects(pure)
{
  count(())
}
